WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.010 --> 00:00:02.710
(NEWSREADER) 'A huge day in prospect at Westminster...'

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:04.660
(POLITICIAN) '...I don't think anybody saw this coming'

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.000
(NEWSREADER) '...about the scale of how bad

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.590
'these growth figures...'

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.580
It's budget day in London, April 22nd,

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.300
and today I have one mission:

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:14.830
which is to get in the background

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:17.290
of as many news camera shots as possible.

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:19.480
There are film crews swarming across the capital.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.800
I've got an Oyster card, a London A to Z...

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.120
There is just one problem.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.700
(LAUGHS)

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.160
I, however, don't need an Oyster card

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.690
because I've got this:

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.600
the Mattmobile.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.040
It's ten o'clock, game's started,

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:35.640
we're kind of stuck in traffic...

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:37.080
'Two hundred miles away,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.120
'a crack team of researchers were watching TV

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.260
'and telling us where the cameras were.'

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.700
How you guys doing up there?

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.670
We're all right!

00:00:43.670 --> 00:00:45.110
Okay, I can barely hear you,

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:46.320
where do I need to go?

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.810
Head across to Westminster.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.900
Right, Westminster.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.220
They've got a camera crew there,

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:54.210
and they're just catching MPs...

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:55.750
They're catching MPs. Parliament Green!

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.630
Okay, thanks Toni, bye bye. Thank you!

00:00:58.630 --> 00:01:00.110
Let's go.

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:02.620
Tom'll be heading into the city now

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.550
on the Underground, probably gaining on us.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.680
But we heard from the command centre earlier

00:01:07.680 --> 00:01:10.240
that one of the tube lines is closed.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:12.700
'Because of industrial action, there is no service

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.580
'in either direction on the Victoria Line.'

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.530
Fantastic! The Victoria line's on strike.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:19.570
How can one tube line go on strike?

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:21.570
(MUSIC: This Morning theme)

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.400
The windows look like grey panes on the outside, don't they?

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:26.260
'I had a plan. And it involved

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:28.630
'getting my face behind Philip Schofield.'

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:32.570
Yeah. There's a lamp post near a circle-y bit, isn't there?

00:01:32.570 --> 00:01:35.030
If I climb that then I should be able to get on it.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:38.520
(TUBE DOORS CLOSE)

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:40.700
Somewhere round here is that bit of green

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.350
that they always interview the politicians on.

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.440
Meanwhile, Matt Gray...

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.760
Matt Gray is stuck somewhere in traffic,

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:49.900
somewhere in London.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:53.420
The magic of London is its road system, which is

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:55.840
built on the Middle Ages(!)

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:57.560
It's actually just a statue

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:00.900
with serieses of traffic lights dotted everywhere

00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:04.150
and you just have to guess!

00:02:04.150 --> 00:02:07.080
I'm kind of wishing I had my Oyster card now.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.960
'The next station is Westminster.'

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.680
'Hello. Are you OK?'

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:15.620
Er, yeah, we are heading towards Blackfriars Bridge

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.710
There were a couple of roads closed that we needed, so...

00:02:19.710 --> 00:02:22.310
Right. It might be worth leaving that

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:23.940
and trying to find somewhere to park

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.030
and heading to Downing Street.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.740
'The command centre were right.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.740
'As I parked, Tom was already at Westminster,

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:32.060
'although running with a backpack in a tube station

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:33.870
'wasn't the smartest thing he's ever done.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:35.450
'I had some ground to make up.'

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:38.700
(MUSIC: BBC News theme)

00:02:38.700 --> 00:02:40.050
Hello, a very good morning to you.

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:42.840
We will of course have all the latest on the Budget...

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.740
'It was a straight race -

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.320
'but I had a mile head start.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:49.110
'And I didn't run like a girl.'

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:50.590
Right there.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:52.400
Right there!

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:55.280
That's them. That's definitely them.

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:57.930
They're live at Westminster on both channels right now.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:02.020
OK! Right, can you see the policeman and the street?

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:05.270
I'm basically behind the BBC setup right now.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.940
You're behind the BBC one? Stay there because

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.080
they will be going back to that after VT.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:13.020
- Here? - They're back on another guy, you need...

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.340
You're in shot!

00:03:15.340 --> 00:03:16.510
You're in shot now!

00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:17.810
Wave!

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:22.590
(MUSIC: Praan by Garry Schyman)

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:23.750
There you go!

00:03:23.750 --> 00:03:24.770
How was that?

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.170
Yes! 20 points!

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:27.370
For about a second...

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:29.830
Okay, let's get to Sky News, let's go!

00:03:29.830 --> 00:03:31.270
'First blood went to me.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:33.460
'I called Matt. Mostly just to gloat.'

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.250
Hello Tom!

00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:35.590
Twenty points!

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:36.660
Twenty? Ah, no...

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:39.120
I was on camera dancing behind BBC news,

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:40.380
so that's 20 points.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:42.190
Right, I'm going to have to go,

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:45.110
I'm too far away now. I'll see you later.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:46.600
See you. Bye bye!

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.040
(MOUTHS) Yes.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.640
'I got there soon after. But not before Tom

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.590
'had spent ten minutes failing to work out

00:03:52.590 --> 00:03:54.400
'where Sky's cameras were pointing.

00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:56.260
I couldn't get it. They're getting wise to this.

00:03:56.260 --> 00:03:57.510
They've moved their cameras

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.860
so they're angling up at people,

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.390
behind Parliament, missing the street.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.600
We're going to have to be very crafty for this one.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.130
Nice glasses.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.290
Cheers.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:08.330
We're going to investigate Downing Street.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.590
I'll see you in a bit.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:10.840
OK, cool.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:11.540
See you.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.860
'The BBC had a camera pointed at the Chancellor's door.

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:15.460
'Sooner or later he'd have to come out

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.060
'and that meant driving out of Downing Street.'

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.130
I'm not allowed down there.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.130
The press are - there's lots of press cameras

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.170
outside Number 10 and 11

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:27.300
and the occasional, um, Cleaning Solutions van.

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.300
I'm assuming that it's actually Cleaning Solutions

00:04:29.300 --> 00:04:31.760
and not some secret government agency.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.760
And now we play the waiting game.

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:35.850
From here in Liverpool, Huw, back to you.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:37.150
Declan Curry there in Liverpool.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:40.590
Now throughout the program, we want to hear from you...

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:43.090
'I don't think they wanted to hear from us.'

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.180
Our political editor Adam Boulton

00:04:45.180 --> 00:04:47.370
is with some of them in Westminster. Adam.

00:04:47.370 --> 00:04:49.500
Yeah, Dermot, you can follow me on Twitter and all,

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:50.380
I don't know how it works

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:51.920
but you can apparently. Anyway.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.770
'Right, we can just see the railings

00:04:53.770 --> 00:04:55.820
'at the very bottom of the shot

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:58.930
'and the police, on their side of the road

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:00.740
You want to be between the bald guy

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.830
and the guy with brown hair.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:05.480
Er - but that's, no, that shot's moved again

00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:07.610
This is bloody Sky, they cannot hold a shot

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:08.640
in the same place.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.750
Look, I Twitter too Adam,

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:10.820
I've got to go back and Twitter

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:12.070
Prime Minister's Questions -

00:05:12.070 --> 00:05:13.930
we're up to date!

00:05:13.930 --> 00:05:15.740
We'll get to see you, but you probably

00:05:15.740 --> 00:05:17.180
can't do anything stupid.

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:19.920
Literally, you get four seconds.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:22.290
'What Tom couldn't do with ten minutes of effort

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:28.000
'I did with two minutes and sheer luck.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:33.900
'Pity I didn't realise it.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:35.480
'And while Tom waited,

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.960
'I got the BBC as well.'

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:38.540
...to tell us what they're expecting. Jon.

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:39.700
Yeah, Huw, a joyous occasion

00:05:39.700 --> 00:05:42.580
not to be freezing on College Green for once(!)

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.120
Ooh. Hello.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:45.790
Another call from the command centre. Hello?

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:47.230
Right, they're live!

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.990
You've got absolutely loads of places

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.760
that you can go here. Er --

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.450
Here's a reminder of the momentous

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.560
economic background to today's budget statement.

00:05:56.560 --> 00:05:59.490
They've just gone to VT. Try and find

00:05:59.490 --> 00:06:02.320
a point where you can see the camera

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:05.200
and - erm - you should be in shot

00:06:05.200 --> 00:06:06.450
at some point.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.400
Yeah. Hang up on me now and save battery

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:09.610
for the both of us.

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:11.280
We're joined now, here, outside Westminster...

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:12.400
There he is!

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:15.370
There - oh - he's on. Yes...

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:18.110
Do something stupid, Matt! I've just hung up!

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:21.960
Do something stupid, you idiot(!)

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:27.910
Oh...

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:29.350
There! Right! Now!

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.370
♪ It's fun to stay at the

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.510
♪ YMCA

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:34.080
♪ It's fun to stay at the

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.780
♪ YMCA... ♪

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:38.080
There you go!

00:06:38.080 --> 00:06:39.660
(LAUGHS)

00:06:39.660 --> 00:06:41.840
Well done Matt, that's 20 points.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:43.090
Hello Matt!

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:43.930
Hello Tom!

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.250
So how are things for you at the moment?

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:48.200
Got any more points(?)

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.410
No, there's nothing going on.

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:51.780
We thought there was a guy with a ladder

00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.400
who was gonna take some video,

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.430
not happening.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:06:55.770
You are on 20 points.

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.090
I am currently on confirmed 30 points.

00:06:58.090 --> 00:06:59.440
Oh, no!

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:01.950
On a BBC interview with Iain Duncan Smith,

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:04.080
I did the YMCA.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:06.780
Okay. See you, Matt...

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.030
See you later, Tom. Good luck.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:12.540
Good luck. Bye bye.

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:15.370
I'm winning.

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:17.180
'And then, to make things worse,

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.990
'the Chancellor took a diversion.'

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:21.690
(REPORTER) Just for those people who are puzzled

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:23.170
by the geography of what we're looking at,

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:24.430
he hasn't gone on to Whitehall,

00:07:24.430 --> 00:07:25.910
he's driven through the archway

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:27.540
of the Foreign Office.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:28.840
They're going to most curious route.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.690
They're going down to the Embankment,

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:32.270
I would hazard a guess.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:35.250
Well - er - anyway, we're going through the back way...

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.410
'With no more points,

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.480
'I headed back to Parliament

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:38.450
'and met up with Matt.'

00:07:38.450 --> 00:07:40.400
You could still get 10 more points

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.300
by doing something stupid behind Sky News.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.050
Yes.

00:07:43.050 --> 00:07:44.670
And I could still get 20 more points

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:45.690
by doing that, which would

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:46.760
put us on a tie.

00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:47.880
I think we're probably standing

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:49.180
in the wrong place.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:51.270
Yes. Our best bet, probably,

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.260
is to go back that way, isn't it?

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:54.560
Let's go.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:56.280
'Then the Chancellor started delivering the budget

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.230
'and the news cameras outside took a break

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.000
'so we did the only thing we could:

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.580
'watched it.'

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.690
(REPORTER) The Chancellor predicts

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:04.500
that the economy is going to shrink by

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.310
three and a half percent this year,

00:08:06.310 --> 00:08:08.820
far worse than previous predictions.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.890
(CHANCELLOR) 'Targeted help to find a new job

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.490
'as quickly as possible...'

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.600
Ow!

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.320
(TOM) 'Matt's balls gave me an idea.'

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:18.810
Let me borrow the balls, please.

00:08:18.810 --> 00:08:19.740
What are you going to do?

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:20.760
Are you going to juggle them

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:21.500
in the background of the shot?

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.680
I want to do that!

00:08:23.680 --> 00:08:25.960
Er, although politically I think it was interesting

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:28.510
how David Cameron, as I predicted...

00:08:28.510 --> 00:08:31.210
Not fair! Not fair!

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:32.550
'It was a valiant effort

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:34.270
'but the Sky News security team

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:36.780
'shut us down very quickly indeed.'

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:38.960
The trouble is, Sky News,

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:41.420
they're angling way too high.

00:08:41.420 --> 00:08:42.910
Way too high up.

00:08:42.910 --> 00:08:44.580
We'd have to climb up...

00:08:44.580 --> 00:08:46.110
'Then I realised the solution

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:49.270
'had been right in front of me.'

00:08:49.270 --> 00:08:52.240
'Abingdon Street.'

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:54.010
I've had the Plan B of getting

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.820
in the background of the London local news

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.260
later on this evening,

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.510
er, hopefully the command centre

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.860
will be able to find me

00:08:59.860 --> 00:09:02.410
a story that's happening in London.

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:03.570
'They could.'

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:06.730
The first Tube strike under Mayor Boris Johnson...

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:07.990
'It was awesome.

00:09:07.990 --> 00:09:09.100
'And it was in the one place that Tom,

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:10.540
'even with his Oyster card,

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:11.560
'couldn't get to.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:13.280
'The Victoria Line.'

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:16.300
To the Mattmobile!

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.160
There is no-one on there...

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.220
'And while Matt drove,

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:20.800
'I did the only thing I could.

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:22.150
'Keep going round,

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:23.640
'and round...

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.630
'and round.'

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:28.000
'The traffic was terrible, even for London.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.490
'Especially for London.

00:09:29.490 --> 00:09:30.700
'Then Tom got a bit of news

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:31.810
'from the command centre.'

00:09:31.810 --> 00:09:32.920
Inside Parliament?

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.220
The BBC are now - hang on -

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.530
let's get this bus!

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:36.730
'The BBC had set up a camera

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:37.990
'in the Central Lobby of Parliament

00:09:37.990 --> 00:09:40.450
'which, technically, is open to the public.'

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:42.030
Right, so it's going to be just me,

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:45.000
going in, and using that... okay. Okay.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:46.160
I can try that.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:48.060
'So I had a decision to make.

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.060
'Stay with the bus, which might never work,

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:51.360
'or try the Central Lobby,

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.270
'which I might never get in to?

00:09:53.270 --> 00:09:55.630
'But as luck would have it,

00:09:55.630 --> 00:09:57.630
'I didn't have to make that choice.'

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:59.210
Here we go, in fact - right now.

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:00.650
I'm right now passing.

00:10:00.650 --> 00:10:03.340
Sky News. Get -- oh, this might work!

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:04.360
This might work!

00:10:04.360 --> 00:10:05.250
Okay, here we go,

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.410
bus is going past...

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.590
er... left, right to left?

00:10:08.590 --> 00:10:10.680
For a long period, er...

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:13.610
(DRAMATIC MUSIC)

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:14.810
...to the left of Labour, er, of

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:16.760
New Labour in power, er...

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:20.710
'And to make it even better,

00:10:20.710 --> 00:10:23.450
'the BBC were live too.'

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:28.140
(MUSIC DROWNS OUT SPEECH)

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.650
That had to have worked.

00:10:30.650 --> 00:10:32.090
Yes!

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:35.250
(MOUTHS)

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:36.500
'Time went on,

00:10:36.500 --> 00:10:38.500
'and our deadline approached.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.240
'Matt had been stuck in traffic jams

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:43.330
'for hours.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.090
'I was waiting in a sweltering,

00:10:45.090 --> 00:10:47.090
'sun-scorched queue.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:49.690
'A reporter missed his entrance.

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:52.800
'BBC cameras were headed to the Victoria line

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.430
'as the command centre

00:10:54.430 --> 00:10:57.720
'desperately tried to plot Matt a route.

00:10:57.720 --> 00:11:00.930
'Could either of us score some final points?'

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:02.830
...in early 2011, they weren't...

00:11:02.830 --> 00:11:05.800
'Yes, I could.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.800
'What you can't see is the three policeman

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.570
'and two security guards ready to arrest me

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:11.330
'if I step out of line,

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:12.630
'so while all I could manage

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.490
'was a sharp salute to camera,

00:11:14.490 --> 00:11:17.180
'it still counted.'

00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:20.990
(BIG BEN CHIMES)

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:22.620
'And that was time.

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.290
'We met up, finally,

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.330
'in a car park on the South Bank.'

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.770
Long day.

00:11:27.770 --> 00:11:28.980
It's been a very long day.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:29.950
Well done, Matt.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:31.630
You've won, haven't you?

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:34.970
I've won. Sorry, Matt.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:39.060
Yet more proof you can't drive round London.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:39.800
Yeah.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.800
(THEY LAUGH)

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:42.860
Let's go to the pub.

00:11:42.860 --> 00:11:43.980
Yeah.

00:11:43.980 --> 00:11:47.140
(ENDING MUSIC)

00:11:47.140 --> 00:11:48.606
Subtitles by Tom Scott

